{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Twelve staffs</b> – The staff of Aaron is one of the twelve, for He did not say, \"and you shall take a staff for the house of Levi and write upon it the name of Aaron,\" but rather it is included in the count mentioned. Now, Joseph is not counted except as one tribe, and the reason is that the tribes of Israel are never counted except as twelve, and since Levi is counted, Joseph is counted as only one. I will further explain this in the portion of VeZot HaBerakhah (Deuteronomy 33:6), if HaShem grants me to reach there." "<b>Each man's name you shall write upon his staff</b> – Some interpret it as the name of the head of the tribe: Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah. But the correct interpretation is the name of the princes, and Aaron is treated as the prince for the tribe of Levi. It was necessary to explain that they are one staff and one prince for them, to say: even though I divided them into two families, the priesthood alone and the Levites alone, nevertheless they are one tribe and have one prince. And the reason is as I explained (Ramban on Numbers 17:6), that no sign was needed other than that that tribe be chosen from all the tribes of Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The verse citation reads דברים ל״ג:ו׳ but the phrase אִם יְבָרְכֵנִי ה׳ may refer to HaShem granting Ramban life to reach that passage in his commentary, not to the cited verse itself."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:34.612531544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}